          <p>
            The adapter you need is always named male first, female second: the male end goes into the outlet, the female end takes your RV's cord. A 50M/30F dogbone lets a 30-amp RV use a 50-amp pedestal. A 15M/30F lets a 30-amp RV plug into a household outlet, which is the "30 amp to 110 adapter" most people search for. A 30M/50F lets a 50-amp RV use a 30-amp pedestal at reduced capacity. Get the direction wrong in the store and the adapter will not fit, which is the safe kind of mistake.
          </p>
